WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:05.050
It's easy to find yourself scrolling through
endless titles on Netflix without ever picking

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:06.050
anything.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.700
But that doesn't mean the streaming platform
has nothing good to offer: you just need to

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.829
know where to look.

00:00:10.829 --> 00:00:14.869
If you're in the mood for a good action movie
you haven't seen a million times, here are

00:00:14.869 --> 00:00:17.900
some hidden gems waiting for you on Netflix.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.289
13 Assassins

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:25.310
If you're a fan of Audition or Ichi the Killer,
here's another classic action movie from Takashi

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:30.410
Miike. 13 Assassins is less brutal than those
earlier films but was favorably compared to

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:34.760
Seven Samurai, which is about the highest
praise a samurai film can get.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.570
Taking place near the sunset of feudal Japan,
a group of samurai gather together to defeat

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:42.170
a sinister lord before he takes the throne.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:47.780
With a 96 percent rating on Rotten Tomatoes,
this might become a new action favorite.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.860
Big Trouble in Little China

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.660
It's hard to go wrong with an '80s action
movie starring Kurt Russell.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:58.410
Big Trouble in Little China stars Russell
as Jack Burton, a man who goes into the mythical

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.670
underworld of Chinatown to save a green-eyed
damsel.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.660
The movie has tons of humor and great '80s
action.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.920
If you like John Carpenter films, especially
Escape from New York, you'll wonder why it's

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.940
taken you so long to watch Big Trouble in
Little China.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.320
Plus it features a great cheesy theme song
from John Carpenter's band.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.870
What's not to love?

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:19.100
Déjà Vu

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.580
Tony Scott didn't always get as much praise
as his older brother Ridley, but he brought

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.150
us some fantastic films.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:31.100
The man behind True Lies and the '80s staple
Top Gun got together an A-list cast for the

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.670
2006 film Deja Vu, an underrated film that
Netflix has been hiding right under your nose.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:41.410
Denzel Washington stars as Doug Carlin, an
investigator tasked with solving a deadly

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.860
bombing in New Orleans.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:47.310
He's given a new piece of technology that
can gaze back four days into the past to help

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:51.830
with the investigation, but he becomes obsessed
with the idea of actually traveling through

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:54.380
time to stop the tragic event from happening.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.229
It's a little sci-fi, a little action, and
all awesome.

00:01:58.229 --> 00:01:59.430
The Hunter

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:03.880
Ever wanted to watch Willem Dafoe hunt for
an extinct tiger in the wilds of Tasmania?

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.200
Well, The Hunter has just made your dreams
come true.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.090
This unusual action film combines science,
exotic locales, and rich character depth to

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.390
create a really intriguing action movie.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:19.029
If you're looking for a slower-paced but extremely
well-acted action adventure, The Hunter is

00:02:19.029 --> 00:02:20.620
just the ticket.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:22.200
Lucky Number Slevin

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.099
This quirky crime comedy flew under the radar
on its release, but Lucky Number Slevin is

00:02:27.099 --> 00:02:31.529
full of twists, turns, and distracting fun
that'll keep you watching to the end.

00:02:31.529 --> 00:02:36.349
It's clever, funny, and has an amazing cast
that includes Morgan Freeman, Bruce Willis,

00:02:36.349 --> 00:02:38.279
Lucy Liu, and Ben Kingsley.

00:02:38.279 --> 00:02:44.260
With a clever script and slick visual style,
Lucky Number Slevin is surprisingly entertaining.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.889
The Finest Hours

00:02:45.889 --> 00:02:51.159
Based on a true story, this tale of a daring
1952 Coast Guard rescue received some pretty

00:02:51.159 --> 00:02:54.889
positive reviews, but kind of sank after its
initial release.

00:02:54.889 --> 00:02:59.769
Maybe because The Finest Hours is pretty generic
for a title, but this real-life tale starring

00:02:59.769 --> 00:03:03.959
Star Trek's Chris Pine is full of thrilling
moments and moving drama.

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:08.749
So before The Finest Hours slips from your
memory again, give this fine historical drama

00:03:08.749 --> 00:03:10.349
a try.

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:11.349
Alive

00:03:11.349 --> 00:03:16.669
This gripping drama is based on the true story
of a Uruguayan rugby team struggling to survive

00:03:16.669 --> 00:03:18.879
in the Andes after a plane crash.

00:03:18.879 --> 00:03:23.439
After only 25 people live through the initial
accident, the team members have to resort

00:03:23.439 --> 00:03:25.650
to desperate measures to stay alive.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:29.739
If you haven't already guessed, yes, this
is the movie where the survivors end up eating

00:03:29.739 --> 00:03:30.739
each other.

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:32.489
But it's not a horror film.

00:03:32.489 --> 00:03:36.480
Watching these people grasp at hope through
the very worst conditions is harrowing, and

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.040
although the movie sounds kind of depressing,
it's actually an uplifting tale of survival

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.790
and the unbelievable strength of mankind — not
to mention a roller coaster ride of sheer

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:47.840
adrenaline.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.079
Super

00:03:49.079 --> 00:03:53.249
Just in case two installments of Guardians
of the Galaxy wasn't enough to satisfy your

00:03:53.249 --> 00:03:57.549
love of James Gunn films, Netflix has a classic
waiting for you.

00:03:57.549 --> 00:04:02.980
Before you watch Super, Gunn's first superhero
film, you should know that it's a dark comedy.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.319
Very dark.

00:04:04.319 --> 00:04:08.199
That said, it's definitely a visually unique
take on superheroes.

00:04:08.199 --> 00:04:12.569
Starring Rainn Wilson and Ellen Page, Super
is about a man who decides to dress up as

00:04:12.569 --> 00:04:17.060
a superhero to save his ex-wife...who doesn't
really want to be saved.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:21.680
It may not have the budget of Guardians, but
you can see Gunn's flare for action and irreverent

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.650
humor shine through.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.110
Trollhunter

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:29.729
This surprisingly unique film follows a group
of people on a quest to find real trolls in

00:04:29.729 --> 00:04:31.780
the frozen tundra of Norway.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:35.400
After they find out that the existence of
trolls has been covered up by the Norwegian

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:40.009
government, they make it their duty to capture
one of the elusive monsters on film.

00:04:40.009 --> 00:04:41.770
This is no Troll 2.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:45.930
These trolls look amazing and don't have to
turn humans into plants to eat them.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:50.860
Shot like a documentary, the film is often
hilarious, though not without its tense moments.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:56.150
Moira MacDonald, film critic at the Seattle
Times, wrote, "Those fog-draped fjords provide

00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:00.819
a distractingly pretty backdrop to this tale
of mysterious, massive creatures who roam

00:05:00.819 --> 00:05:04.539
the forest by night, searching for Christians
on whom to munch."

00:05:04.539 --> 00:05:08.300
It's safe to say that you're not going to
find a better movie about massive monsters

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.550
eating religious folk.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:11.860
Zombeavers

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:16.680
Don't worry: Zombeavers is completely aware
that it's a movie about zombie beavers.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:21.139
Thankfully, it's a fun horror parody that
makes the idea of undead beavers as funny

00:05:21.139 --> 00:05:22.680
as it could possibly be.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:27.010
Critic Tim Brayton called it "the funniest
horror-comedy since, at the very least, The

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.409
Cabin in the Woods."

00:05:28.409 --> 00:05:33.310
If you want a campy, diverting comedy that's
full of laughs and gross-out gags, Zombeavers

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.690
is exactly what you're looking for.

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:37.659
Welcome to the Punch

00:05:37.659 --> 00:05:41.780
Starring Mark Strong and James McAvoy star
as a criminal and cop who team up to uncover

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:46.419
a conspiracy, Welcome to the Punch is straight-up
action in the best possible way.

00:05:46.419 --> 00:05:51.349
The solid casting choices lend a bit of seriousness
and depth of character to the story, but let's

00:05:51.349 --> 00:05:55.669
all be honest: this is a movie you watch for
awesome chase scenes and gun fights.

00:05:55.669 --> 00:05:59.669
Welcome to the Punch is pretty violent, but
you'd probably expect that from a film that

00:05:59.669 --> 00:06:02.360
invites you to a beating in the title.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.659
Last Knights

00:06:03.659 --> 00:06:08.639
A cast that stars Clive Owen and Morgan Freeman
usually means a movie worth watching.

00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:13.430
Add in castles, swords, and revenge, and you
have yourself a fine action film.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:17.639
Now, the critics weren't especially kind to
Last Knights, but the New York Times thought

00:06:17.639 --> 00:06:22.630
Bonnie and Clyde was an overly violent, pointless
piece of cinema, so why listen to critics?

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:26.789
Last Knights probably won't stand the test
of time like Bonnie and Clyde, but if Game

00:06:26.789 --> 00:06:31.090
of Thrones reruns aren't doing it for you,
or if you just like hearing the soothing tones

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:35.599
of Morgan Freeman while people are killed
with swords, Last Knights is worth a watch.

00:06:35.599 --> 00:06:37.240
Thanks for watching!

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:40.189
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:40.189 --> 00:06:42.599
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

